A||||10||GTMike||heat wraping exaust and intake???||||1||
Z||000000||GTMike||07-26-2001||01:35 AM||||i was thinking of useing heat wraping stuff one my maniflods and my cross over pipe.  <P>also i was thinking of doing a cold air induction.  keeping the rubber elbo   but getting rid of every thing else.  useing a str8 pipe to get a cone filter outside the engine compartment  and in to the wheel well. and then heat wrapinging the pipe and the elbo.  i think this would reduce the intake air temp.  what do you guys think of this set up???||||reg||1
Z||000001||elfiero||07-26-2001||08:34 AM||||Yes it will lower the air temp as measured<BR>at the throttlebody.But the question is how<BR>much horsepower is it worth?-the answer is<BR>not enough to go to all that much work!Buy<BR>a K&N air intake setup instad.much more<BR>improvement!||||reg||6
Z||000002||GTMike||07-26-2001||04:30 PM||||it will basically be an k&n intake system. i will use a cone k&n filter outside the eng. compartment.   i will not bue useing any of the stock air box stuff. just the rubber elbo.  then heat wraping the hole thing. so it will be the intake system  and it will be heat wraped   so it will be much colder. i guessing it will be a few more hps over just the k&n system alone. heat wraping the intake and the exaust should keep all that extra air cold instead of getting heated up as it passes over the cross over pipe.<P>any one else have opinions??||||reg||1
Z||000003||Neal||07-26-2001||06:41 PM||||If ya wanna do it, do it.<P>there will be no ill effects from wrapping the intake, however the amount of time the air spends in the intake is so little i dont think that wrapping it would produce any extra hp.  And if the exaust was wrapped i think it would be worth anything to wrap the intake.||||reg||1
Z||000004||West Coast Fiero||07-26-2001||07:05 PM||||if interested - we have done the homework for you, we offer a Cold Air Intake specificaly for the V6 Fiero, check out our page...<BR> <A HREF="http://www.cwestco.com" TARGET=_blank>www.cwestco.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||GTMike||07-27-2001||12:39 AM||||i did a search and looked at how others have done the cold air intake and  all you need is the cone k&n and a boom tube crome exaust tip and some hose clamps to get the intake its pretty much the same as  west coast think except for like 50 bucks. <P>so wraping the intake wouldn't do anything at all??   <P>but wraping the exaust would help...<P>i guess i wont wrap the intake. <P>thanks||||reg||1
Z||000006||WKDFIRO||07-28-2001||12:23 PM||||But as has been mentioned many, many, many times before, the cost of wrapping your exhaust may be more than what you pay in wrap. The wrap will also trap moisture and pretty much destroy your exhaust tubing. Wrapping in many articles has been recommended only for stainless steel exhaust. The rusting involved is not worth the exhaust leaks.||||reg||2
Z||000007||cadaver||07-29-2001||12:26 AM||||Never wrap your pipes.||||reg||1
Z||000008||GTMike||07-30-2001||05:09 PM||||thanks guys  i learn something new every day.  i wont wrap my pipes.<P>thank. ||||reg||1
